// @test regression/INV138-collection-receiver-valid
// @description The valid counterpart to INV138-collection-receiver-method-call, TV-clean (probed p10, 2026-07-15): builtin members reached in method form on array/map/matrix receivers, plus a user `method` extending `array<float>`. The user-method hatch is what INV065 meant by collection methods being "user-extendable"; it is covered by the same name-only `declaredFunctionNames` check the scalar slice uses.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects errors: 0
//@version=6
indicator("x")
method scale(array<float> this, float k) =>
    for [i, v] in this
        this.set(i, v * k)
    this
arr = array.new<float>(0)
m = map.new<string, float>()
mx = matrix.new<float>(2, 2, 0.0)
arr.push(1.0)
arr.scale(2.0)
m.put("a", 1.0)
mx.set(0, 0, 1.0)
plot(arr.size() + m.size() + mx.rows())
